  "releaseNotes": "Enhancements\n- Added support for reading four-digit ITF barcodes when ITF is the only type specified in `ExpectBarcodeTypes`.\n\nBug Fixes\n- Fixed an issue where ITF barcodes could be missed during full-page scans when other content followed them on the same line. Improved detection of slanted ITF barcodes and reduced false positives.\n- Fixed an issue where `ReadingSpeed.Detailed` and `ReadingSpeed.ExtremeDetail`, when used with `ExpectMultipleBarcodes`, could miss barcodes detectable only with certain image filters. Results are now combined across filters, which may increase scanning time.\n- Fixed inconsistent results in Detailed and ExtremeDetail scanning when using `Multithreaded`, including skipped image filters in single-threaded mode and failure to respect `MaxParallelThreads`.\n- Fixed an issue where invalid barcode results could prevent valid barcodes from being returned.\n- Fixed incorrect position reporting for truncated PDF417 barcodes and improved handling of malformed GS1 DataBar barcodes.\n- Fixed an issue where barcode creation could fail due to non-critical warnings.\n\nUpdates\n- Updated GS1 human-readable text formatting to support the latest Application Identifier definitions.\n- Updated internal dependencies.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": true,
  "title": "IronBarCode Detection - An advanced package that leverages Machine Learning for more accurate BarCode detection.",
